# Backend Conventions

## Services
- Concrete scoped classes in `Infrastructure/Services/` (no interfaces unless required)
- Inject `AppDbContext`; use `AsNoTracking()` for reads
- Map large responses via `ProjectRows` + in-memory `ToDto` (named properties); small lookups may still project directly
- Business rule failures: `throw new InvalidOperationException("پیام فارسی")` → controller returns `BadRequest`
- Stamp `CreatedById` / `UpdatedById` from caller's user id
- Respect soft delete — do not hard-delete auditable entities

## Contracts (Core) — Request vs Response
- **Requests:** `*Request` positional `record` + DataAnnotations; Persian `ErrorMessage`
- **Responses:** `*Response` — never `*Dto`
  - Auditable: extend `ResponseBase` (`Audit` + `CloneResponse` / `WithoutAudit` once — do not redeclare Audit)
  - With attachments: extend `AttachmentResponseBase` (`Attachments` + `ApplyVisibility` / `WithoutAttachments`)
  - Markers: bases implement `IHasAudit` / `IHasAttachments`
  - Small (≤5 fields): positional `record` OK (`LookupItemResponse`, `TransactionAttachmentResponse`, small reports)
- **Visibility:** static `ResponseVisibility.Apply<T>()` / `ApplyAttachments<T>()` — deep-clone via `ExpressionDeepClone`, never mutate cache (not DI)
- Password fields: `[PasswordStrength]` → `PasswordPolicy` (min 6, letter, digit, symbol)
- Optional password on update: `[PasswordStrength(AllowEmpty = true)]`

## Service projections
- Prefer **slim SQL row** (`ProjectRows` → EF `Select` with named property init) then **in-memory `ToDto`/`ToResponse`**
- Computed display names: `PersonDisplayNameHelper` in Core — do **not** concat prefix/first/last in SQL
- Audit: project username/avatar scalars onto the row; assemble with `AuditHelper.FromProjection` in memory
- Never mutate FusionCache response instances — strip on a deep clone only

## Controllers (Api)
- Extend `ApiControllerBase`; keep thin — delegate to services
- Shape permission-gated fields via static `ResponseVisibility.Apply<T>` / `ApplyAttachments<T>`
- Gate with `[RequirePermission(PermissionCodes.X)]` (OR logic for multiple codes)
- `[Authorize]` on controller; `[AllowAnonymous]` only on login
- Multipart transactions: JSON in `data` form field + optional **`documents`** files (same field name, multiple files)
- Per-attachment delete: `DELETE {income|cost}-transactions/{id}/attachments/{attachmentId}` — requires `attachments.delete` **and** module `*.update`; delete file via `FileStorageService.TryDelete`

## Transaction attachments
- Entity: `TransactionAttachment` (`Path`, FK to income or cost transaction)
- Response: `attachments: [{ id, path }]` — stripped when caller lacks `attachments.view`
- Permissions (no menu): `attachments.view` | `attachments.add` | `attachments.delete`
- Response: `audit: { createdAt, createdBy, createdByAvatarPath, updatedAt, updatedBy, updatedByAvatarPath }` — stripped when caller lacks `audit.view` via static `ResponseVisibility` (Api layer; not Infrastructure)
- Permission (no menu): `audit.view`
- Uploading `documents` on create/update requires `attachments.add`
- FK delete behavior: **`Restrict`** (not Cascade) — SQL Server multiple-cascade-path limitation
- Attachments removed individually in service; soft-deleted transactions keep attachment rows

## System admin guards
```csharp
if (SystemUsers.IsSystemAdmin(entity.Username))
    throw new InvalidOperationException("...");
```
Apply on user delete/update/password/avatar for admin account.

## Caching
- Lookup reads: FusionCache via `LookupCache` TTLs; call invalidation helpers after writes

## Lookups API (form reference data)
- **`GET /api/lookups/accounts`** — `{ id, name }[]`; allowed with `accounts.view` **or** any income/cost view/create/update
- **`GET /api/lookups/cost-types`** — `{ id, name, unitName? }[]`; allowed with `costtypes.view` **or** income/cost/food view/create/update
- **`GET /api/lookups/persons`** — paged PersonSelect search; ALL tokens match FirstName/LastName/NickName of person + father + mother; FusionCache slim list + in-memory filter (includes `IsDead`; **no** `DeathDate`); invalidate with LookupCache.InvalidatePersonsAsync
- **`GET /api/reports/death-anniversaries?scope=Day|Week|Month|Season&referenceDate=`** — `[RequirePermission(PermissionCodes.DeathAnniversariesView)]` (`deathanniversaries.view`); deceased persons whose Jalali death anniversary matches reference; week = Sat–Fri containing reference
- Admin list APIs (`/api/accounts`, `/api/cost-types`) stay behind module `*.view` for CRUD pages only
- `LookupService` + separate cache keys; invalidated with account/cost-type/person writes

## Migrations
- Add EF migration in Infrastructure; applied automatically at startup via `DbSeeder`
